    "body": "## Motivation\n\n#41520 states that only the finishing insert bumps `hit_count` and that checkpoints do not. The `cache_inserted_len` watermark it landed with also bumps hits on checkpoint inserts, so with `write_through_threshold=1` the HiCache write-through / external-linker offload fires once per prefill chunk instead of once per request. With the UMBP linker on a PD prefill this roughly doubles the number of offload batches and slows decode steps by ~2 ms at 1e86143b.\n\n## Modifications\n\n`UnifiedRadixCache.checkpoint_into_tree`: pass `inserted_len=0` for a finished request (each node on the path counts once) and the full key length for a checkpoint (no node counts). Prompt-split re-inserts and `RadixCache` are unchanged.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nN/A: only changes when hit counters are bumped (and thus when write-through/offload is triggered); the model forward and the inserted KV are unchanged.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nDeepSeek-V4-Pro FP4, 1P1D on MI355X: prefill TP8/EP8 with the UMBP linker (`write_through`), decode TP8 with DP attention, DSPARK, agentic workload at concurrency 256, 3600 s. Each column uses one fixed node pair. Decode step time in ms, regressed to 16 running req/rank and 220k context.\n\n| sglang | Pair A | Pair B |\n|---|---|---|\n| before #41520 ¹ | 48.59 | 48.44 |\n| #41520 ² | 49.83 | 50.29 |\n| 1e86143b (main, Oct 7) | 49.3–50.0 (4 runs) | 49.7–50.2 (2 runs) |\n| 1e86143b + this PR | **47.52** | **47.64** |\n\n¹ Pair A at 2a3655fea1, Pair B at bf8adf9602 (runtime-identical to the parent of #41520).\n² Pair A at 1db33bc367 (only a NIXL change after #41520), Pair B at 50be533d09.\n\nPrefill UMBP offload entries per batch (all ranks): 1.88 with #41520 vs 3.38–3.63 with this PR (3.46 before #41520); total offloads unchanged (~94k per run). Prefill prefix-cache hit rate unchanged (96.5%). Output throughput +1.2% (A) / +1.4% (B) vs the mean of the 1e86143b runs (61.1k / 61.0k tok/s). Runs used an equivalent sentinel (`1 << 62`) for the checkpoint `inserted_len`.\n\nThe existing `test_scripted_core_1gpu` hit-count tests expect every node to be hit exactly once after the request finishes, which still holds (not run locally).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [ ] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39032825640](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39032825640)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39032825599](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39032825599)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39032825575](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39032825575)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
