      "patch": "@@ -237,7 +237,7 @@ Insert a request's KV into the tree: at every checkpoint while it runs, and once\n \n | Aspect | Detail |\n |--------|--------|\n-| **Purpose** | Publish the request's KV `[cache_protected_len, up_to)` so other requests can match it; nodes past `req.kv.cache_inserted_len` count one hit (a request counts each node once). `checkpoint_kv_cache` calls it with `req.extend_end` while the request runs; `release_kv_cache` calls it with the request-owned length when it finishes (`req.finished()`), then frees `[cache_protected_len, up_to)` and everything past it and unlocks `req.lock`; with `checkpoint=False` it skips the insert and calls `on_release(req, checkpointed=False)` for component cleanup |\n+| **Purpose** | Publish the request's KV `[cache_protected_len, up_to)` so other requests can match it; only the finishing insert counts hits, one per node on the path (a checkpoint counts none). `checkpoint_kv_cache` calls it with `req.extend_end` while the request runs; `release_kv_cache` calls it with the request-owned length when it finishes (`req.finished()`), then frees `[cache_protected_len, up_to)` and everything past it and unlocks `req.lock`; with `checkpoint=False` it skips the insert and calls `on_release(req, checkpointed=False)` for component cleanup |\n | **Inputs** | `req` — the request; `up_to` — row position the insert may read up to |\n | **Output** | `None` |\n | **Mutation** | Component hooks → `insert` → re-match → writes the tree's indices back into the row → moves `req.lock` to the node the insert ended on → updates `req.kv.cache_protected_len`, `req.kv.cache_inserted_len`, `req.last_node` (`checkpoint_kv_cache` then advances `req.prefix_len`) → component cleanup. A finished request's component state (Mamba) is handed to the tree instead of forked, and what it still held is freed. Frees no KV slot: `release_kv_cache` does that afterwards. |",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/raw/92545f2e4cae2bd516393d9a4a7a785fdd124aea/python%2Fsglang%2Fsrt%2Fmem_cache%2Funified_cache%2Fcomponents%2FREADME.md",
      "sha": "4c258df6ed9a45e6ae445e1909b41a2274d0ddae",
      "status": "modified"
    },
    {
      "additions": 4,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/92545f2e4cae2bd516393d9a4a7a785fdd124aea/python%2Fsglang%2Fsrt%2Fmem_cache%2Funified_radix_cache.py",
      "changes": 5,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/contents/python%2Fsglang%2Fsrt%2Fmem_cache%2Funified_radix_cache.py?ref=92545f2e4cae2bd516393d9a4a7a785fdd124aea",
      "deletions": 1,
      "filename": "python/sglang/srt/mem_cache/unified_radix_cache.py",
      "patch": "@@ -1140,10 +1140,13 @@ def checkpoint_into_tree(self, req: Req, *, up_to: int, **kwargs) -> None:\n             req.kv.req_pool_idx, : len(token_ids)\n         ]\n \n+        # Only the finishing insert counts hits, once per node on the path; a\n+        # checkpoint (e.g. a prefill chunk) counts none, so write-through and\n+        # external-linker offload fire once per request rather than per chunk.\n         # components prepare insert data + return effective cache_len\n         insert_params = InsertParams(\n             prev_prefix_len=req.kv.cache_protected_len,\n-            inserted_len=req.kv.cache_inserted_len,\n+            inserted_len=0 if is_finished else len(token_ids),\n             priority=req.priority or 0,\n             session_id=req.session_id,\n             rotation_base=req.kv_rotation_base,",
